+# Audit #1690 Evidence Dossier — License Contract Mismatch (2026-10-30)
+
+**Report-only, keep-open.** #1690 is a licensing **owner decision**; this dossier
+verifies the mismatch is still live on every cited surface and stages both
+sanctioned remedies. No agent can legitimately choose between "gateway is
+public" and "gateway is proprietary" — that call reclassifies intellectual
+property.
+
+## Live state verified 2026-10-30 ~22:00 UTC (zero-credential probes)
+
+| Surface | #1690 claim | Live probe | Verdict |
+| --- | --- | --- | --- |
+| `gateway/LICENSE` (open repo) | MIT (c) 2026 | 1074 bytes, "MIT License, Copyright (c) 2026 SaifulHaque Niloy" | **still MIT** |
+| `Supremeai-bd/supremeai-api` head | no license | `licenseVerdict: unknown/no-license` (repo info probe) | **still unlicensed** |
+| `ECOSYSTEM_MAP.md` §2.3 (L48) | MIT strictly `open`/`studio`/`vscode` | unchanged | **api excluded from MIT** |
+| `ECOSYSTEM_MAP.md` §2.3 (L49) | api = Proprietary ("provider gateway") | unchanged | **api in proprietary list** |
+| Routing matrix | `gateway/**` → api satellite | `scripts/bridge/bridge_intake.py` `route_files()`: `gateway/` prefix → `Supremeai-bd/supremeai-api` | **confirmed** |
+| Public exposure | mirror ships implementation | `git ls-files 'gateway/'` = **324 files** incl. Dockerfile, CI, full Python implementation | **confirmed** |
+
+The four operator commits referencing #1690 (2026-10-27, "replace gateway/LICENSE
+MIT with proprietary notice", "proprietary LICENSE notices for mirror surfaces")
+did **not** reach the open-repo `gateway/LICENSE` or the api satellite head —
+both still show the pre-fix state, so the finding is **not stale** (U3 verified).
+
+## The mismatch, stated once
+
+The public boundary currently distributes 324 gateway files under an MIT grant,
+while the SSOT map classifies the same subsystem as Private · Proprietary with
+only contracts public in open. Depending on which surface a court or a
+downstream consumer reads first, the federation either grants perpetual
+MIT rights to the whole gateway or forbids its reproduction entirely. Both
+documents claim to be the contract; they cannot both be right.
+
+## Remedies (verbatim from #1690, decision belongs to the owner)
+
+1. **Gateway is a public boundary** → update `ECOSYSTEM_MAP.md` §2.3 + the api
+   repo description to declare the gateway mirror MIT; keep satellite internals
+   proprietary below the contract surface.
+   - Consequence: the map's MIT list grows by one; 324 already-public files
+     become legitimately MIT; zero deletion work; the "moat" moves to the
+     private-side gateway internals.
+2. **Gateway is proprietary** → replace `gateway/LICENSE` with the standard
+   proprietary notice and expose only `api-schemas/*` + client examples per the
+   map's "(Contracts public in open)" note.
+   - Consequence: the MIT grant is revoked *after* it was public — existing
+     forks/clients hold MIT copies from the grant window regardless; requires
+     an exposure review (what shipped, for how long) and moving non-contract
+     files out of the public boundary; larger remediation surface.
+
+**Observed operator signal** (not a decision): the 2026-10-27 commit titles
+lean toward remedy 2. If remedy 2 is confirmed, the open-repo change is a
+single-file `gateway/LICENSE` swap (agent-lane, `baseSha`-carried full_file
+order) plus a follow-up scoping decision on the other 323 files that needs its
+own admin ruling before any deletion order is filed.
+
+## Why report-only
+
+Both remedies mutate a legal grant. Picking one autonomously would make the
+agent a licensing authority, which no bridge rule delegates. The honest
+agent-lane deliverable is verified evidence + staged options; this report is
+that deliverable. Recommend labelling #1690 for admin decision; the live probes
+above can be re-run byte-for-byte to confirm either fix lands.
